# p1s-ca.pem — TEMPLATE (do not commit the real file)
#
# The real `p1s-ca.pem` is the captured TLS chain from a SPECIFIC printer:
# the leaf cert's Subject CN is that unit's serial, and it regenerates on
# every firmware update. It is printer-specific and sensitive — it is
# .gitignored. Each implementer derives their own at runtime; this is also
# exactly the serial-from-cert-CN onboarding step.
#
# Derive (CLI, for reference / debugging):
#   echo | openssl s_client -showcerts -connect <PRINTER_IP>:8883 2>/dev/null \
#     | awk '/-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----/,/-----END CERTIFICATE-----/{print}' \
#     > p1s-ca.pem
#   openssl x509 -in p1s-ca.pem -noout -subject   # subject=CN=<SERIAL>
#
# In the app: open a TLS socket to ip:8883, read the peer cert
# (getpeercert(binary_form=True)), parse the CN = serial, and TOFU-pin the
# leaf fingerprint keyed by that serial (re-prompt on change; never pin BBL CA).
# See CONNECTING.md §1–2, SYNTHESIS §2.2, recommend-aragorn-2026-05-19.md §2.
#
# Expected structure (two PEM blocks): leaf (CN=<serial>) then BBL CA.
-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
<printer leaf cert — CN is the unit serial; captured at runtime>
-----END CERTIFICATE-----
-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
<BBL CA — O="BBL Technologies Co., Ltd", CN="BBL CA" (shared; never pin)>
-----END CERTIFICATE-----
